disgraced celebrity lawyer michael  avenatti sentenced to two and a half  years in jail  for scheme related to suing nike if you  don't recall michael avenatti  represented a putative whistleblower who  said that nike was paying high school  and college students  to sign nike endorsement deals which was  of course illegal but the problem for  avenatti is that not only was he trying  to get money for his client he was also  trying to get money for himself he tried  to extort nike for  millions of dollars so that he could run  an internal investigation  of nike's practices and he'd get paid as  a consultant pro tip as a lawyer you are  not allowed to do that  so a jury convicted avenatti on three  counts related to extortion  interstate communications related to  extortion and wire fraud and he now has  been sentenced to two and a half years  in jail  and on top of that he faces other  charges in california where he could  face even more time in jail so  we're definitely going to see michael  avenatti in court
 

